Bugs Ubisoft never patched, fixed in the running game. Nothing on disk is overwritten, nothing is left behind when you remove it, and it works alongside the data mods you already have.

[size=4][b]What it fixes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Jackal tapes[/b] - in the southern map the same tape, usually #09. Stealing Boots, played on every pickup. They advance through the set again.[/*]
[*][b]Predecessor tapes[/b] - the seven Intel Bonus missions are back. They ship with the game but sat behind an ownership check that can no longer succeed.[/*]
[*][b]Machetes[/b] - the Primitive and Homemade machetes are back, the same way. Pick one in [b]Options → Game → Machete Type[/b].[/*]
[*][b]Exit crash[/b] - quitting through Exit Game closes the game instead of crashing it.[/*]
[*][b]Mouse speed cap[/b] - a fast flick no longer turns the view less far than a slow one.[/*]
[*][b]Slow loading screens[/b] - they run at the 30 FPS they were paced for.[/*]
[*][b]Grass under spot lights[/b] - headlights and flashlights light the grass they shine on.[/*]
[*][b]CPU and GPU use[/b] - the engine uses every processor it has and stops wasting a whole core on its own frame cap.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Settings[/size][/b]
In [b]Options → Mod Configuration Menu[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Field of view[/b] - 65 to 140 degrees for the view on foot. Default 75, the game's own. It applies in cutscenes, scripted animations and on ladders too. Sights, scopes and vehicles keep their own, and an arms dealer's computer shows the game's own view.[/*]
[*][b]Maximum frame rate[/b] - 60 Hz by default, since the game's physics misbehave above it. Also unlocked, your screen's refresh rate, or 30 to 240 Hz.[/*]
[*][b]Display mode[/b] - borderless, from the next launch.[/*]
[*][b]Processor affinity[/b] - fewer cores, the old workaround for NPCs bouncing on machines with many cores. Costs performance.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]How to install (Vortex)[/size][/b]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/about/vortex/]Vortex[/url] and its Far Cry 2 extension.[/*]
[*]Click [b]Mod Manager Download[/b] on this page and enable the mod. Vortex also offers to get [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url], which this mod needs.[/*]
[*]Start the game with the [b]Play[/b] button in Vortex.[/*]
[/list]
Not using Vortex? Install it with JackAll instead, [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url] for JackAll installation. Or by hand: copy [font=Courier New]plugins\UFCP.dll[/font] into the game's [font=Courier New]bin\plugins[/font] folder and start the game with [font=Courier New]FCSE.exe[/font].

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Needs Far Cry 2 patch 1.03[/b], Steam or GOG, and FCSE 1.4.0 or later.[/*]
[*][b]Don't use it together with FC2JackalFix or FoxAhead's Multi Fixer.[/b] They patch the same code.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]bin\fcse.log[/font] lists every fix that was applied.[/*]
[/list]
